    **BLOCKED 2026-07-22** at Step 1 (coverage check) — the 006 Phase-0 gate is confirmed GREEN, but
    `collectEditedParagraphs`'s whole-paragraph delete/merge sentinel (`docxBridge.ts:360-368`, emits
    `{paraId,text:''}` so the server synthesizer strikes a vanished paragraph — the UAT-round-4
    "vanished paragraph" corruption fix) has NO equivalent in the task-020/022 step interceptor today:
    `classifyStep` explicitly defers every structural step (split/merge/insert/delete paragraph) to
    task 031 (`🔲 not-started`, `blocked` in TASK-INDEX, deps on 030 which is also not-started), and
    `onStructuralStep` has zero wired handlers in production (`ComposeEditor.tsx`/`ComposeWorkspace.tsx`
    register the interceptor bare). Deleting `collectEditedParagraphs` now would silently and
    permanently drop this case (no flag, no signal — not even the "captured but deferred" seam is wired).
    Full analysis + 3 resolution options (A: re-sequence dep on 031 [recommended]; B: documented interim
    exception per root §6.5; C: pull forward minimal structural capture) in
    `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/BLOCKED.md`. No code was changed under this task — `docxBridge.ts`,
    `ComposeWorkspace.tsx`, `ComposeEditor.tsx`, `index.ts` are untouched.
